  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Evrysdi (risdiplam) / Spinraza (nusinersen). Version: 1; Original: 2/15/2022; Approval: 9/16/2022; Effective: 11/1/2022.",
    "Encoded: closed product and SMA indication lists, approval criteria 1–6 and denial criteria 2–3. Denial 1 is failure to meet approval criteria. Spinraza is labeled for pediatric and adult patients without a minimum age in this PDF; Evrysdi requires age ≥2 months, represented as 2/12 years.",
    "Baseline motor assessment and the infant under 1 month deferral are combined attestations; documentation requires manual review. Contraception counseling applies to both products for females of reproductive potential.",
    "Cautions (notes only): see the Evrysdi and Spinraza package inserts.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 6 months; reauthorization up to 12 months if the prescriber documents improvement or stability from baseline.",
    "Quantity (notes only): Evrysdi 0.2 mg/kg once daily if age <2 years; 0.25 mg/kg once daily if age ≥2 years and weight <20 kg; 5 mg once daily if age ≥2 years and weight ≥20 kg.",
    "Quantity (notes only): Spinraza 12 mg (5 mL) per administration; four loading doses, first three at 14-day intervals and fourth 30 days after third; maintenance every 4 months thereafter. HCPCS J2326.",
    "Zolgensma is a separately encoded SMA gene replacement therapy alternative, not a product in this pack. Prior SMA gene replacement therapy excludes eligibility here. Alternative eligibility requires separate evaluation.",
    "Duration, renewal response, quantity and cautions remain notes only, so this pack remains partial. PDL status remains unknown."
  ],
